'# A record field can have a default value (`field : Type ?? default`) or be' Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

'# optional (`field ?: Type`). Both let you leave the field out when you build the record.' Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

'# A defaulted field is always there when you read it, so you read it with plain `.field`.' Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

'# An optional field may be missing, so you read it with `.?field`, which gives you a `Try`.' Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

"# Defaults are only allowed on a nominal (`:=`) type declaration's backing record," Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

'# so every construction that omits a defaulted field is an explicit `ServerConfig.{...}`.' Comment.Single
'\n'          Text.Whitespace

